56 153Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E3-MJMAIN-38\" d=\"M70 417T70 494T124 618T248 666Q319 666 374 624T429 515Q429 485 418 459T392 417T361 389T335 371T324 363L338 354Q352 344 366 334T382 323Q457 264 457 174Q457 95 399 37T249 -22Q159 -22 101 29T43 155Q43 263 172 335L154 348Q133 361 127 368Q70 417 70 494ZM286 386L292 390Q298 394 301 396T311 403T323 413T334 425T345 438T355 454T364 471T369 491T371 513Q371 556 342 586T275 624Q268 625 242 625Q201 625 165 599T128 534Q128 511 141 492T167 463T217 431Q224 426 228 424L286 386ZM250 21Q308 21 350 55T392 137Q392 154 387 169T375 194T353 216T330 234T301 253T274 270Q260 279 244 289T218 306L210 311Q204 311 181 294T133 239T107 157Q107 98 150 60T250 21Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-31\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-30\" x=\"500\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-35\" x=\"1001\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use transform=\"scale(0.707)\" xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-2218\" x=\"2123\" y=\"583\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-2B\" x=\"2177\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<g transform=\"translate(3178,0)\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-37\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-35\" x=\"500\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use transform=\"scale(0.707)\" xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-2218\" x=\"1415\" y=\"583\"></use>\n</g>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-3D\" x=\"4911\" y=\"0\"></use>\n<g transform=\"translate(5967,0)\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-31\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-38\" x=\"500\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-30\" x=\"1001\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use transform=\"scale(0.707)\" xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-2218\" x=\"2123\" y=\"583\"></use>\n</g>\n</g>\n</svg></span></p>\n<p>A <strong>linear pair</strong> is a pair of adjacent angles formed when two lines intersect. The angles shown above form a linear pair.</p>\n<p>The <strong>linear pair postulate</strong> states the following:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If two angles form a linear pair, then they are supplementary.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The converse is <em>not</em> true. That is, if two angles are supplementary, they do not necessarily form a linear pair.</p>\n<p>To see why, consider the diagram shown below:</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-690283fc338c98fc275550b19e00d5ce\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/690283fc338c98fc275550b19e00d5ce\"></div>\n\n<p>Although the angles are supplementary (the sum of their measures is <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"18.401ex\" height=\"2.343ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.505ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 7922.7 1008.6\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-4-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-4-Title\">120^\\circ + 60^\\circ = 180^\\circ</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E4-MJMAIN-31\" d=\"M213 578L200 573Q186 568 160 563T102 556H83V602H102Q149 604 189 617T245 641T273 663Q275 666 285 666Q294 666 302 660V361L303 61Q310 54 315 52T339 48T401 46H427V0H416Q395 3 257 3Q121 3 100 0H88V46H114Q136 46 152 46T177 47T193 50T201 52T207 57T213 61V578Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E4-MJMAIN-32\" d=\"M109 429Q82 429 66 447T50 491Q50 562 103 614T235 666Q326 666 387 610T449 465Q449 422 429 383T381 315T301 241Q265 210 201 149L142 93L218 92Q375 92 385 97Q392 99 409 186V189H449V186Q448 183 436 95T421 3V0H50V19V31Q50 38 56 46T86 81Q115 113 136 137Q145 147 170 174T204 211T233 244T261 278T284 308T305 340T320 369T333 401T340 431T343 464Q343 527 309 573T212 619Q179 619 154 602T119 569T109 550Q109 549 114 549Q132 549 151 535T170 489Q170 464 154 447T109 429Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E4-MJMAIN-30\" d=\"M96 585Q152 666 249 666Q297 666 345 640T423 548Q460 465 460 320Q460 165 417 83Q397 41 362 16T301 -15T250 -22Q224 -22 198 -16T137 16T82 83Q39 165 39 320Q39 494 96 585ZM321 597Q291 629 250 629Q208 629 178 597Q153 5